## 3. Frameworks & Libraries

### UI and build

- **Framework:** React 19
- **Routing:** React Router v7 (React Router 7)
- **Build:** Vite 7
- **Bundler:** Vite (default)

### Styling stack

- **Tailwind CSS v4** (with `@tailwindcss/vite` and `@tailwindcss/postcss`)
- **Shared theme:** `@vtrip/tailwind-config/theme` — imported in app CSS, not via `tailwind.config.js`
- **Utilities:** `tailwind-merge`, `clsx` (via `cn()`)
- **Component variants:** `class-variance-authority` (cva)
- **Icons:** `lucide-react` + custom SVG icons in `packages/ui/src/icons/`

### App entry and CSS

- **Web apps:** `apps/{app_name}` (main app currently `apps/web`)
- **Root:** `apps/{app_name}/app/root.tsx` (e.g. `apps/web/app/root.tsx`) — imports `./app.css`
- **Global CSS:** `apps/{app_name}/app/app.css` (e.g. `apps/web/app/app.css`) — must `@import "@vtrip/tailwind-config/theme"` and `@source` the UI package for Tailwind content
- When implementing a design, always confirm which `apps/{app_name}` you are modifying.

