## 6. Styling Approach

### Methodology

- **Utility-first:** Tailwind v4 with shared theme. No CSS Modules or Styled Components; use Tailwind classes and `cn()` for composition.
- **Theme consumption:** Tokens are in `tooling/tailwind/theme.css`. Apps import it via:

  ```css
  @import "tailwindcss";
  @import "@vtrip/tailwind-config/theme";
  ```

- **Tailwind content:** App CSS uses `@source "../../../packages/ui/src/**/*.{ts,tsx}"` so classes used in `packages/ui` are generated. Do not add a separate `content` array in a config file; Tailwind v4 uses `@source` in CSS.

### Global styles

- **App entry:** `apps/web/app/app.css`
- **Base layer:** `@layer base` in that file sets `:root { --font-geist-sans: "Inter Variable"; }`, `* { @apply border-border; }`, `body { letter-spacing: var(--tracking-normal); }`.
- **Font:** `@import "@fontsource-variable/inter";` (Inter Variable).
- **Dark/light:** Custom variants: `@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *));` (and `light`, `auto`). Use `dark:` prefixed utilities for dark mode.

### Responsive design

- Use Tailwind breakpoint prefixes: `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, etc. Container uses `--theme(--breakpoint-sm)` in media queries:

  ```css
  @utility container {
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: 2rem;
    @media (width >= --theme(--breakpoint-sm)) {
      max-width: none;
    }
    @media (width >= 1400px) {
      max-width: 1400px;
    }
  }
  ```

- Prefer semantic tokens (e.g. `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `rounded-lg`) over raw hex or arbitrary values when matching Figma.

